## Audit / gate posture

- Audits are evidence-based against live `next.` + git tip; do not claim GO if deploy ≠ commit, ops unverified, or DB down.
- npm audit: safe patch OK (e.g. Next 15.5.28); **do not** `npm audit fix --force` (Next 16 / zod 4) on cutover day.
- Remaining GO blockers for real production cutover: VPS backup off-box, formal smoke logged, env (`AUTH_*`, Postgres not public), Cloudflare Full (strict), and clean CF cache policy — many are VPS/`LAUNCH.md` ops, separate from laptop tunnel UAT.
- DNS cutover to apex must not happen until a clean release artifact + ops checklist; leave public DNS on current site until then.

